-- title:
--   Inverse module of a principal product of Cartier divisors is trivial
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme and let $\iota$ be a finite index type. Let $C : \iota \to X.\mathrm{IdealSheafData}$ be a family of quasi-coherent ideal sheaf data on $X$, each of which is invertible in the sense of `IsInvertible`: for every $i$ and every point $x$ of $X$ there is an affine open $U$ and a section $f \in \Gamma(X, U)$ with $x$ in the basic open $X.\mathrm{basicOpen}\, f$, together with a non-zero-divisor $g \in \Gamma(X, X.\mathrm{affineBasicOpen}\, f)$ such that the ideal cut out by $C\,i$ on $X.\mathrm{affineBasicOpen}\, f$ is the principal ideal $\mathrm{span}\{g\}$. Let $\mathrm{mult} : \iota \to \mathbb{N}$ be multiplicities, and let $t$ be an endomorphism of the unit object $\mathbf{1}$ of the monoidal category $X.\mathrm{Modules}$ of sheaves of modules on $X$, i.e. a global section of the structure sheaf. Assume $\prod_i (C\,i)^{\mathrm{mult}\, i}$, the product taken in the multiplicative monoid of ideal sheaf data, equals the zero-scheme ideal $\mathrm{zeroSchemeIdeal}\ t$, that is the infimum of those $J$ with $\mathrm{coeffIdeal}\ t\ U \le J.\mathrm{ideal}\ U$ for all affine opens $U$, where $\mathrm{coeffIdeal}$ is spanned by the coefficients of $t$. Then the type of isomorphisms $\bigl(\prod_i (C\,i)^{\mathrm{mult}\, i}\bigr).\mathrm{invModule} \cong \mathbf{1}$ in $X.\mathrm{Modules}$ is nonempty, where $\mathrm{invModule}\ I$ denotes the internal dual $(\mathrm{ihom}\ I.\mathrm{module}).\mathrm{obj}\ \mathbf{1}$ of the ideal $I.\mathrm{module}$, itself the kernel of the unit-to-pushforward-unit map of the closed immersion attached to $I$.
--
--   This is the single relation among the classes of the components of a special fibre: if $\sum_i m_i C_i$ is the divisor of a global function, then $\mathcal{O}_X(\sum_i m_i C_i) = (\prod_i C_i^{m_i})^{-1}$ is trivial, so the classes $[\mathcal{O}(C_i)]$ satisfy $\sum_i m_i[\mathcal{O}(C_i)] = 0$ in the Picard group. No hypothesis on $X$ beyond invertibility of the $C_i$ is imposed. It is used in the computation of relative Picard groups of glued smooth curves and in the identification of the line bundles attached to products of invertible ideals generated by a single section.
-- source:
